<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mohammed al-Shaykh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1490">1490</a>–<a href="/years/1557">1557</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mohammed al-Shaykh was the Saadi sultan who united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> under his dynasty. He captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agadir">Agadir</a> from the Portuguese in 1541 and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> from the Wattasid Sultanate in 1549, ruling the whole country from then until 1557. He resisted Ottoman ambitions in Morocco and was assassinated by an Ottoman agent in 1557.</p></div>
